  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Security posture",
      "items": [
        "Loopback-only bind (127.0.0.1) with a DNS-rebinding-safe Host/Origin guard on every HTTP request and the WS upgrade; the server is .unref()'d and never keeps the process alive.",
        "Every /files response carries Content-Security-Policy: sandbox allow-scripts allow-downloads (opaque origin — the document can never reach /api or the WS endpoint same-origin) plus X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff.",
        "Containment mirrors /output: decode-after-strip, NUL reject, realpathSync both sides, regular files only — traversal, symlink hop, escape, and missing file are all the SAME uniform 404 that never leaks existence."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "v3 — pure HITL companion",
      "items": [
        "t02 frame diet at the SOURCE: message_*, tool_execution_*, tool_result, turn_*, agent_settled, session_*compact are never subscribed — the store, the wire, and the shell all stay lean; the TUI owns logs.",
        "t03 shell rebuild: the transcript scrollback machinery is deleted (−68 lines); three tabs — Inbox (ask + event cards, boot default), Report, Data (viewer) — with #card-<id> deep links that activate the owning tab. Post-t03 hardening (#1576/#1577): the html-report iframe is properly sized (70vh — it was the 300x150 browser default) with a fullscreen escape hatch, and the shell is a dynamic 100dvh app-shell — panes fill any browser size, no fixed caps.",
        "D1 decision: the webui is a pure interaction surface. No chat composer, no log mirror — answers flow back through the appexec bridge, first-answer-wins, queued while offline."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Report — two doors, one archive",
      "items": [
        "Producers: the webui_report tool (in-process, zero sockets) and POST /api/report (external) converge on ONE shared builder (report-frame.ts) — byte-identical frames: title 1–200, exactly-one body mode, 16MB cap (v3 follow-up #1573).",
        "Store-wrapped broadcast: live delivery + replay append; report frames are EXEMPT from the bounded card-eviction cap — the Report tab is the durable archive surface.",
        "Markdown renders via the DOM-built renderer; HTML renders in a sandboxed iframe — the same trust boundary as /files, inside the tab."
      ]
    }
  ]
